course: dictionary
lesson: 1272
title: Busk and its two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives busk two: the usual meaning, and an informal one, busk it. The words around busk tell you which meaning is used. «Busking means performing in public places for tips» is about playing music or singing in a street for money from people who pass by.
explain: Look for clue words. In «many famous musicians busked when they started», the word started tells you that busking is something musicians often do when they are beginners, in public places. Always ask: does my meaning fit this sentence?
explain: Busk it is informal. If a friend says, «I haven't learnt the song, so I'll just busk it», the words haven't learnt are the clue. The friend means they will do it without preparing, and make it up as they go.
fact: To busk means to play music, sing, juggle or perform in a public place, such as a street or station, for money from people passing by.
fact: A person who busks is called a busker.
fact: Buskers often ask for money by leaving a hat or guitar case open for coins.
fact: Some places need a permit before you can busk, so the rules matter.
fact: Informally, «busk it» means to do something without preparing, or to improvise.
exercise: «Busking means performing in public places for tips.» What does busk mean? | To shop for bargains in a busy market | To hide from people | *To perform in a public place for money from people passing by | To sleep outside in a tent
exercise: Ella says, «I haven't practised, so I'll just busk it.» What does busk it mean here? | To go to bed early | To write a letter | *To do it without preparing | To buy a new guitar
exercise: Which word means a person who plays music in the street for money? | blanket | *busker | banker | builder
test: Where do buskers often perform? | At the bottom of the sea | In a library, quietly reading | *In town centres and underground stations | In a bakery kitchen
test: What does a permit for busking show? | Every shop is closed | *The place has rules, and you need permission | Everyone is paid a salary | The park gates are locked
exam: Which sentence uses busk in its informal sense? | *She had no notes, so she decided to busk her speech | The busker played his guitar by the station | Many famous musicians busked when they started | People dropped coins into the busker's hat
